# 6 Sep 2026. Forward from 2dc9472a, which was pinned on 3 September and has
# been overtaken by ten merges. Diffed as a parsed schema tree rather than as
# text, because the last two defects on this document were both YAML that
# parsed cleanly into the wrong place (yuvoy-api#92, #103): the change is
# PURELY ADDITIVE — twenty new schema paths, nothing removed, nothing retyped.
#
# Consumed in this change (yuvoy-app#18):
#   - `GET /reels` — the feed. `/v1/experiences` returns one listing per row
#     with a single `heroMedia` each, so the number of reels a traveller could
#     see was capped at the number of listings however much operators filmed.
#     Two visible against three published, and the third had been invisible
#     since the day it went up.
#   - `ExperienceSummary.seatsOnNextDisplay` — the seat sentence, decided
#     server-side. Fixes yuvoy-api#92, where it had been swallowed into
#     `BookingMode`'s description and was not a field at all. The card had been
#     printing "N seats left" below a threshold IT kept, which is a second copy
#     of a rule the server owns; that copy is now deleted.
#   - `OperatorSummary.logoUrl` — shown where a listing has no reel of its own.
#
# Landed and NOT consumed, each needing its own issue before anything is built:
#   - `BookingStatus.meetingPoint` / `.cancellation` / `.requestExpiresAt`
#   - `ReservationContact.marketingConsent`
#
# Known gap, raised rather than papered over: `GET /reels` takes `limit`
# (1–60, default 30) and returns no cursor, so the feed is one page and stops
# at 60. Fine at three reels; not fine later. Raised on yuvoy-api rather than
# faking pagination client-side, because a client that invents paging over an
# unpaged endpoint re-requests the same rows.
